==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈwɜːkɪŋ/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈwɝkɪŋ/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-working.ogg|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)kɪŋ|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|work|ing}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|werking}}, {{m|enm|werkynge}}, {{m|enm|warkynge}}, {{m|enm|worchinge}}, from {{inh|en|ang|wyrċing|t=working}}, verbal noun of {{m|ang|wyrċan|t=to work}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|work|ing}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|wirking}}, {{m|sco|warking}}, {{cog|nl|werking}}, {{cog|de|Wirkung}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|usually|in the plural}} [[operation|Operation]]; [[action]].
# [[method|Method]] of operation.
# {{lb|en|arithmetic}} The [[incidental]] or [[subsidiary]] [[calculation]]s performed in solving an overall [[problem]].
#: {{ux|en|Be sure to check your '''working'''.}}
# [[fermentation|Fermentation]].
# (of bodies of water) Becoming full of a [[vegetable]] [[substance]].
# A place where work is carried on.
#: {{ux|en|the abandoned mine '''workings'''}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A train movement.

